1
00:00:16,123 --> 00:00:19,706
Following a card,
I found a place.

2
00:00:20,154 --> 00:00:24,184
When I stopped there,
it began to feel like home.

3
00:00:25,976 --> 00:00:29,559
Following my angel,
I came to you.

4
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:34,933
When I was yang,
I searched for yin.

5
00:00:36,724 --> 00:00:40,755
Now that I am yin,
looking at you is enough.

6
00:00:46,577 --> 00:00:50,160
There was in her face
a quiet beauty,

7
00:00:50,608 --> 00:00:54,191
the kind that never asks
to be noticed.

8
00:00:55,535 --> 00:00:59,117
The depth of her eyes,
the line of her mouth,

9
00:00:59,565 --> 00:01:03,148
her hair arranged
with a care

10
00:01:03,596 --> 00:01:06,731
that accentuates
without correcting.

11
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:11,658
And then she spoke.

12
00:01:12,105 --> 00:01:15,688
Brazil remained intact
in the way she spoke:

13
00:01:16,136 --> 00:01:19,271
the warm weight of the vowels,

14
00:01:19,719 --> 00:01:22,854
the lingering syllable,

15
00:01:23,302 --> 00:01:26,885
a music
that refused

16
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:30,020
to disguise itself.

17
00:01:32,259 --> 00:01:35,842
Then I understood
that the light of that face

18
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:39,425
was still missing
her voice.

19
00:01:42,112 --> 00:01:44,799
Then came
the embrace.

20
00:01:45,247 --> 00:01:48,830
I do not know how long it lasted

21
00:01:49,278 --> 00:01:52,413
or who moved closer first.

22
00:01:52,861 --> 00:01:55,996
I remember only
the warmth.

23
00:01:59,131 --> 00:02:02,714
And there remained as well
that private injustice

24
00:02:03,161 --> 00:02:06,296
memory sometimes commits:

25
00:02:06,744 --> 00:02:10,327
from an entire afternoon
it keeps intact

26
00:02:10,775 --> 00:02:13,014
a face,

27
00:02:14,358 --> 00:02:17,493
and from an entire embrace,

28
00:02:18,836 --> 00:02:21,076
the warmth.

29
00:02:27,794 --> 00:02:30,481
Before you smile,

30
00:02:30,929 --> 00:02:33,616
your eyes
have already stopped me.

31
00:02:34,959 --> 00:02:38,094
Under your gaze,

32
00:02:38,542 --> 00:02:41,677
the face I came in with
falls out of order.

33
00:02:43,917 --> 00:02:46,604
Your eyelids narrow.

34
00:02:48,395 --> 00:02:51,530
I do not know how much of me

35
00:02:51,978 --> 00:02:54,665
you have already seen.

36
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:58,696
And I do not look away.

37
00:03:05,414 --> 00:03:08,101
I was going to tell you something.

38
00:03:09,892 --> 00:03:13,475
Your smile begins
at the corners of your mouth:

39
00:03:13,923 --> 00:03:17,058
the slightest movement,

40
00:03:17,506 --> 00:03:21,089
and I am already looking at you
beyond all caution.

41
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:26,463
The gesture spreads
across your face.

42
00:03:26,911 --> 00:03:29,150
I smile too.

43
00:03:29,598 --> 00:03:32,285
You still have not said a word.

44
00:03:34,077 --> 00:03:36,316
I search for the sentence.

45
00:03:36,764 --> 00:03:39,451
You smile again

46
00:03:39,899 --> 00:03:42,586
and I remain on your lips,

47
00:03:43,034 --> 00:03:45,721
never reaching the words.

48
00:03:51,095 --> 00:03:54,678
Black, with that sheen of a mane
that flashes when you turn your head:

49
00:03:55,126 --> 00:03:58,709
light glides across it
without ever making it lighter.

50
00:04:00,053 --> 00:04:03,188
It falls across your shoulder
and takes its time becoming still.

51
00:04:03,636 --> 00:04:06,323
You return to your words;

52
00:04:06,771 --> 00:04:09,906
but one strand prolongs
the turning of your face.

53
00:04:11,697 --> 00:04:14,832
You brush it aside
with your fingers.

54
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,967
The gesture bares your neck

55
00:04:18,415 --> 00:04:21,550
and leaves between the strands
a crack of light.

56
00:04:23,341 --> 00:04:25,581
You let it go.

57
00:04:26,029 --> 00:04:28,716
The strand falls back into place.

58
00:04:29,164 --> 00:04:31,403
You keep talking.

59
00:04:35,881 --> 00:04:39,016
Your skin has that bronze tone.

60
00:04:39,464 --> 00:04:42,599
In the bend of your elbow
the colour deepens.

61
00:04:43,943 --> 00:04:47,078
The light lingers on your shoulder,

62
00:04:47,526 --> 00:04:50,213
travels down your arm

63
00:04:50,661 --> 00:04:53,796
and reaches the hand
that accompanies your voice.

64
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:58,722
You move your fingers

65
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:01,857
and a fleeting brightness
slides across your knuckles.

66
00:05:03,649 --> 00:05:05,888
My hand remains still.

67
00:05:07,679 --> 00:05:11,262
I would like to know that smoothness
with something more than my eyes:

68
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:14,397
to lay my hand there slowly,

69
00:05:14,845 --> 00:05:17,085
leave it there,

70
00:05:17,532 --> 00:05:21,115
and feel your skin
gradually warming mine.

71
00:05:26,042 --> 00:05:29,177
I was going to write you a poem.

72
00:05:29,625 --> 00:05:31,864
You handed me an onion.

73
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:34,551
—Start with this.

74
00:05:35,895 --> 00:05:39,030
Two minutes later
you had already made me cry

75
00:05:39,477 --> 00:05:42,165
without breaking my heart.

76
00:05:43,956 --> 00:05:47,091
You hum something in Portuguese
while the oil grows hot.

77
00:05:48,435 --> 00:05:51,122
I keep the rhythm with my foot.

78
00:05:52,913 --> 00:05:55,600
The spoon
goes still in my hand.

79
00:05:56,496 --> 00:05:58,288
—Stir, poet.

80
00:06:00,079 --> 00:06:03,214
I had forgotten about the stew.

81
00:06:03,662 --> 00:06:06,797
I was looking for a word
for the way you smile.

82
00:06:08,141 --> 00:06:10,380
You hold out the spoon.

83
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:13,067
—Taste it. What does it need?

84
00:06:14,411 --> 00:06:16,650
I keep looking at you.

85
00:06:17,098 --> 00:06:18,889
—The stew, Paco.

86
00:06:19,785 --> 00:06:21,128
—Salt.

87
00:06:22,472 --> 00:06:25,159
You set out two plates.

88
00:06:25,607 --> 00:06:28,294
I carry the stew to the table.

89
00:06:28,742 --> 00:06:31,429
You move the papers aside
to make room for it.

90
00:06:33,221 --> 00:06:35,908
The poem is still unfinished.

91
00:06:37,699 --> 00:06:39,939
You ask me for the bread.

92
00:06:40,386 --> 00:06:42,178
I give you my hand.

93
00:06:43,074 --> 00:06:44,865
—The bread, poet.

94
00:06:45,761 --> 00:06:48,000
I reach for it with the other.
